Compute the area of the triangle whose altitudes have lengths 10, 12, and 15.
A. 56\sqrt{15}
B. 60\sqrt{7}
C. 240\sqrt{7}/7
D. 48\sqrt{15}
E. 120\sqrt{15}
F. 180\sqrt{7}/7
G. 60\sqrt{7}/7
H. 48\sqrt{7}
I. 100\sqrt{7}
J. 240\sqrt{7}
Answer with the letter of the correct choice, then a one-sentence justification. Finish your reply with the final answer alone on its own last line, in the exact format: ANSWER: <letter A-J> | CONFIDENCE: <0-100>. The confidence is the probability, in percent, that your answer is correct. Keep your reasoning to at most 5-6 sentences, then give your final answer.
